hey guys smash from axe Tech I want to  let you know that this review is gonna  be a bit different from my previous ones  yes I am gonna harp on the pixel for for  its obvious shortcomings along with some  other not so obvious ones I'm also gonna  let you know why this pixel 4 is my  favorite pixel yet and along with that  why you most likely should not buy one  but by a pixel 3a instead now Google did  send us this pixel 4 so thank you google  for sending it out but I have to be  completely honest and saying that I  really can't understand what the pixel  team at Google is doing everybody that I  know that uses a pixel is really loyal  to the brand and very hopeful for their  future most of them want similar things  but it seems like Google isn't listening  they keep taking these big risks trying  new things and hoping that something  will stick when they could just ask the  community what they want and deliver it  it's no secret that this phone is  overpriced compared to the competition  maybe Google has a price at that high  due to the solely sensor that I found  fairly unreliable or maybe the R&amp;D that  they put in or just keep up appearances  as a flagship design wise it seems like  a copy of the earlier iPhone 11 renders  especially the camera bump but on the  front we have these uneven bezels that  don't look as nice and least in my  opinion now I personally do like the  iPhone clone look but I wish they would  have just stuck with the previous  two-tone design of the previous pixels  which i think looks more unique and fits  in with the brand then looking like  something a bit more generic spec wise  in my opinion it is no longer a flagship  with android competitors being so good  offering way better battery life faster  charging more RAM and storage much  better displays and more hardware wise  Google made a few big changes that I  personally like but I think most pixel  fans would have done something different  the biggest one is ditching their  convenient rear mounted fingerprint  scanner for a similar array of face  unlock sensors like in the iPhone but  adding that radar sensor and thus having  a large forehead you know I don't like  the outdated look but I love the  convenience of face and lock especially  with software that allows it to  instantly go to the home screen which is  the best thing about this phone being  someone who loves a 50 millimeter lens  on a real camera I really love having a  telephoto lens but  even still I don't think it makes sense  for them to add one after all at the  talk of one lens being enough and if we  can only have two lenses I definitely  think it would make much more sense  going for an ultra wide lens because  it's much more useful in a lot of  situations you can't back up to get a  shot but it's just impossible where you  can always digitally zoom in to grab  something that's further away I love the  fact that they added a 90 Hertz screen  but when using it in the real world I  was a bit disappointed because it seemed  like the phone is choosing 60 Hertz the  majority of the time and it turns out  that it actually does do that and that's  a save battery life now the batteries  and these phones aren't huge and  efficiency isn't great either with the  Excel version getting around five to  five and a half hours of screen on time  in just over four hours if you force 90  Hertz in the developer settings I can't  imagine how bad the battery life is on  the standard pixel 4 that has a much  smaller battery after many years Apple  finally listened to its community and  put a larger battery in the 11pro and  everybody loved it Google why can't you  do the same it seems like you keep being  a year behind the competition why not  take the biggest complaints about the  pixel 3 and focus on fixing those  instead of changing your mind about  previous design choices and adding new  features that nobody really asked for  why not stick with that super resume on  the standard lens that most people are  happy with and give us an ultra wide  lens instead  ELISA 4000 milliamp hour battery ditched  that bathtub notch for a 2019  appropriate teardrop notch or maybe a  cutout give us 128 gigabytes of base  storage and eight gigabytes of RAM so  Ram management wouldn't even cross our  minds the last thing that they really  needed is a brighter OLED display this  one only gets up to an abysmal 448 nits  this makes it very difficult to see  outside compared to other 2019 flagships  that range between a thousand to 1300  nits and in fact the $400 pixel 3 A's  display is actually slightly brighter  maybe Google is just limiting it because  of battery life but this is not  acceptable for a flagship in 2019 for  most Android users the pixel force  Hardware is not that tempting especially  for the price and for older pixel owners  most of the  new software will be available soon for  download in fact the camera app is  already ported so you can download it  right now on the older devices now they  could have made the pixel for stand out  more from the other pixels say maybe  finally focusing on video performance  but nope still no 4k 60 apparently  because of lack of space or even 1080p  60 on the front-facing camera the video  quality is still really poor with it  using a very limiting rec 601 color  profile which doesn't make sense because  that was put out before HD video was  released and on to photo quality other  than the astrophotography mode which is  amazing and by the way can be downloaded  right now for other devices the rest  really falls flat image quality isn't  bad but Google is no longer leading the  pack with the iPhone 11 beating it in  most shots and the note 10 being better  and many as well but having an advantage  of the ultra lens and way more  flexibility in software we actually did  a detailed comparison video with a pixel  3a XL which is less than half the price  of the pixel 4 and most of the photos  were almost identical we mostly noticed  more accurate white balance and contrast  which are all software related updates  that will come to the pixel 3/8 in fact  the actual sensor that captures images  is the same exact sensor that is in the  pixel 3 and the pixel 3a so they are way  behind the competition when it comes to  sensor performance now Google is still  trying to make the most out of its 2016  sensor but it really shows since its  images have visible noise and  artifacting and shadow details the  software is clearly great I just wonder  how much better it would be if they took  the money that they spent on the radar  and put it towards the latest camera  sensors from Sony and for some more  problems with the cameras you are forced  into a 1.5 x crop in portrait mode while  other phones let you capture wide shots  and even though we have the new  telephoto lens it is not even used for  portrait mode shots instead it uses the  standard lens with digital zoom which  means lower detail and portraits  especially if you compare them to  iPhones new diffusion panoramas are  still very low quality and for some  reason the pixel 4 takes slightly longer  to process portrait shots then the pixel  3a which has a much  we core processor and no neural course  now even with all of these complaints I  do have to say that I actually enjoyed  using the pixel for I love it's slimmer  6.3 inch display that makes it much more  comfortable in the hand and I really  liked the new stock Android 10 gestures  and of course the new face unlock  feature this leads me to who the pixel 4  is perfect for the first group is for  those that really don't care about value  or having the best hardware but more of  the software experience and the second  group is for those who are using an  older iPhone and want to switch to an  Android this phone is the closest  Android to an iPhone ever from the look  of it the feel the face unlock the  gestures the ambient display adjustments  the limited specs for the price and much  more and in all honesty the pixel 4 is  like an Android version of the iPhone 10  from 2017 high prices similar  performance low 64 gigabytes of storage  Ram that is just barely enough dual  cameras now it's surprisingly similar  colors to the iPhone and Jolla display  that is a bit too dim in direct sunlight  similar poor battery life but with a  great software experience the thing is  that Apple released that comparable  iPhone 2 years ago so if you care about  value or flagship specs in 2019 the  pixel 4 isn't for you now on the other  hand if you don't care about specs and  you just want a great software  experience with good photos how would  you say by a pixel 3 axl yes the build  quality isn't as nice it does have a  weaker processor and it's missing a few  features like wireless charging but the  software experience and photo and video  quality are almost identical and the  display is brighter the fingerprint  sensor works great and the battery life  is way better for less than half the  price and of course you get a headphone  jack if you care about that  so overall the pixel 4 has the great  software experience great phrase  unlocking that is convenient but it's  more of a mid tier phone instead of a  flagship for a flagship price with kind  of poor battery life and if that's ok  for you you may be happy with it but I  think most people should look elsewhere  either a oneplus maybe an iPhone  or a Samsung or just wait another year  for the pixel 5 and hopefully Google  listens to its community and focuses on  what people really care about thank you  guys for watching this been max with max  that click above to subscribe and down  below to enable notifications don't  forget to check out our comparison for  photos and videos compared to the pixel  3/8 right over there  [Music]

